A||N||4||FieroJoe||Wheel locks||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||01-02-2001||09:14 PM||||What years were wheel locks an availible option, and does anyone have a pic of what they look like?<BR><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-02-2001||09:35 PM||||every year that had AL wheels far as I know.<P>They look like the rest of the lug nuts except the top is round with notches cut in it instead of hex shaped. They take the same little plastic covers on them as the OE lugnuts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||01-03-2001||02:13 AM||||I think I have a set of the original wheel locks with the key. Just don't have the plastic covers.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||01-03-2001||10:12 AM||||Well, so now I know that I have factory wheel locks, they match your description.<P>I have the lock too, thankfully.  I just thought that they might be some aftermarket add-on||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||01-03-2001||08:07 PM||||That I know of only McGard and the company GM contracted for the OE ones make locks that use the plastic caps. All others I've seen are full lug style. <P>If you have the lock number stuck in the spare tire bay or someplace else you can order extra keys. NIFE has an article that explains who to call and how to ID you locks if you don't have the number. <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-lugpanic.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-lugpanic.html</A> <P><A HREF="http://www.mcguard.com/" TARGET=_blank>McGard</A> is the only maker I'd use for replacements. Pretty much everything besides them and Amcor aren't worth a dime.||||reg||1
